  "aboutHeading": "What a service visit actually includes",
  "about": "Most people meet their spa company once and never see the same face again. That is how a tub ends up with cloudy water, a waterlogged cover and a heater nobody looked at until January.\n\nEvery visit is the same list, every time, and it takes about half an hour. You get a photo of the water and the chemistry readings on your phone before we drive away — so you know we came, and you know exactly where your water stands.\n\nThe tub is the thing you actually use in a Nebraska winter, so spa service runs all year. Pools run on the season, and the opening and closing visits either side of it are the two that matter most — a pool closed properly in October is a pool that costs nothing in April.",
